<title>SOUTH KOREA: Hotel Shilla says buying back shares.</title>
<headline>Hotel Shilla says buying back shares.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hotel Shilla said on Saturday it would buy back 364,836 common shares and 15,037 preferred shares on the open market to boost share prices between Jan 29 and April 28.</p>
<p>Hotel Shilla holds none of its own shares now.</p>
<p>A company statement said the purchases would be made at the closing price of the previous day.</p>
<p>Hotel Shilla shares closed 400 won higher at 7,000 on Saturday.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5645</p>
</text>
